---
source: tests/golden/harness.rs
---
  x modules source `tectonic-os` is declared twice
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-sources/repo.kdl:5:13]
  4 | sources {
  5 |     modules "tectonic-os" {
    :             ^^^^^^|^^^^^^
    :                   `-- first here
  6 |         url "https://github.com/tectonic-os/modules"
  7 |         version "v1.0.0"
  8 |         sha256 "b7c232b0e8249d8e55a40beb79c5c43a7d370f3f9408bd215deb0170daeaadf3"
  9 |     }
 10 |     modules "tectonic-os" {
    :             ^^^^^^|^^^^^^
    :                   `-- and again here
 11 |         dir "../modules"
    `----
  help: one kind and alias identify one source; merge the fields or rename one
        declaration

  x invalid modules source name `Scratch`
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-sources/repo.kdl:13:13]
 12 |     }
 13 |     modules "Scratch" {
    :             ^^^^|^^^^
    :                 `-- lowercase, digits and dashes, starting with a letter
 14 |         dir "../modules"
    `----
  help: the alias qualifies references and names its local cache

  x `local` is a local directory
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-sources/repo.kdl:18:9]
 17 |         dir "../modules"
 18 |         version "v1.0.0"
    :         ^^^|^^^
    :            `-- only a Git source accepts this field
 19 |     }
    `----
  help: a local source needs only `dir`; pinning fields describe a fetched
        repository

  x `bare` needs one source location
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-sources/repo.kdl:20:13]
 19 |     }
 20 |     modules "bare" {}
    :             ^^^|^^
    :                `-- pick `dir` or `url`
 21 |     modules "insecure" {
    `----
  help: a local source declares `dir`; a fetched source declares `url`, not
        both

  x `insecure` does not use an HTTPS Git URL
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-sources/repo.kdl:22:9]
 21 |     modules "insecure" {
 22 |         url "http://github.com/tectonic-os/modules"
    :         ^|^
    :          `-- not HTTPS
 23 |     }
    `----
  help: `url "https://host/owner/repository"`; credentials and host policy
        stay with Git
